      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "638151e96969f673b29911a6",
      "mergedPostDetails": "It works if you add the Audio Listener to a separate object from the reference camera and add the Audio Reverb Filter to it.\nBut it's inconvenient and should be fixed.\nSDK Version 2021.06.03.14.57",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Audio Reverb Filter doesn't work when it is added to reference camera in SDK3.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5fa7c1daaf245e2d67aaf768",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have researched this issue with this topic owner and will provide more detailed information below.\n- There was a known bug in SDK3 where the \"Audio Reverb filter\" (for voice echo) did not work.\n- In this time, We ware able to find out the conditions under which it stopped working.\n・\"Audio Reverb filter\" does not work if the \"Audio Listener\" is specified as the Reference Camera in \"VRCWorld\" prefab.\nIn the initial state of Unity's Scene, the \"Audio Listener\" is originally attached to the Main Camera, and in many cases, the Main Camera is  attached to the Reference Camera in world creation in order to set the \"Post Processing\" settings and the \"culling distance between players\" (it called \"loving distance\" in Japanese).\nFor this reason, the Audio Reverb filter has been thought to be non-functional.\nSo now, the smartest way to work around this bug is to remove the \"Audio Lisnter\" from the Main Camera and attach the \"Audio Listner“ and ”Audio Reverb filter“ to a new, empty object.\nOnce this SDK3 bug is fixed, we can attach the \"Audio Reverb filter\" directly to the Reference Camera, and it should work (as you expected).\n(Here is a canny that reported the same phenomenon regarding player voice with a similar component.)\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/audio-reverb-zone-stopped-echoing-back-the-players-voice-in-recent-bulild",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
